\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {S.13}{\ignorespaces All-pairs correlation, five-nearest-neighbor prediction and activity cliffs for every representation in each regression dataset's pool. All pairs: Spearman correlation between pair distance and absolute label difference, on a fixed sample of 2,000 molecules (seed 0) where a dataset has more. Five neighbors: Spearman correlation and RMSE (in the label's units) of the mean label of the five nearest molecules from other scaffold groups. Cliff molecules: molecules in at least one of this representation's closest pairs whose labels differ by more than the dataset's gap (Table~\ref {tab:flaws:distance_summary}). The number of closest pairs is the number ECFP4 has at Tanimoto $\geq 0.55$, a few more where distances tie at the cut-off. Shared: percentage of ECFP4's similar pairs that are also among this representation's closest pairs. HLM clearance's pool has no ECFP4.}}{36}{table.1.13}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:flaws:distance_per_rep}{{S.13}{36}{All-pairs correlation, five-nearest-neighbor prediction and activity cliffs for every representation in each regression dataset's pool. All pairs: Spearman correlation between pair distance and absolute label difference, on a fixed sample of 2,000 molecules (seed 0) where a dataset has more. Five neighbors: Spearman correlation and RMSE (in the label's units) of the mean label of the five nearest molecules from other scaffold groups. Cliff molecules: molecules in at least one of this representation's closest pairs whose labels differ by more than the dataset's gap (Table~\ref {tab:flaws:distance_summary}). The number of closest pairs is the number ECFP4 has at Tanimoto $\geq 0.55$, a few more where distances tie at the cut-off. Shared: percentage of ECFP4's similar pairs that are also among this representation's closest pairs. HLM clearance's pool has no ECFP4}{table.1.13}{}}
