\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {S.16}{\ignorespaces Number of configurations in one search over every value of the search settings. A configuration is one choice of downstream model, internal evaluator, allocation method, importance method, representation count and budget. Each (downstream model, internal evaluator) pair runs 5 allocation methods $\times $ 3 importance methods $\times $ 4 representation counts $\times $ 8 budgets $= 480$ configurations (Table~\ref {tab:search_tiers}). ``Matched'' is counted once where it repeats an evaluator already in the list. Each configuration is scored on 5 folds, so five downstream models mean 40{,}800 fits of a downstream model.}}{40}{table.caption.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:add:search_size}{{S.16}{40}{Number of configurations in one search over every value of the search settings. A configuration is one choice of downstream model, internal evaluator, allocation method, importance method, representation count and budget. Each (downstream model, internal evaluator) pair runs 5 allocation methods $\times $ 3 importance methods $\times $ 4 representation counts $\times $ 8 budgets $= 480$ configurations (Table~\ref {tab:search_tiers}). ``Matched'' is counted once where it repeats an evaluator already in the list. Each configuration is scored on 5 folds, so five downstream models mean 40{,}800 fits of a downstream model}{table.caption.3}{}}
