\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {S.19}{\ignorespaces Fields a blueprint saves. The stored score of each representation is its best score on its own across the downstream models, over every molecule the search ran on. It is not the internal-evaluator score that splits the budget, which a rebuild computes again on the molecules it is given. Two further fields are read only by allocation or augmentation routes outside the thesis's search and are fixed: a minimum improvement a whole block of extra features must show (none) and a number of features taken from each source (20).}}{48}{table.1.19}\protected@file@percent }
